# Strings that are DELIBERATELY not translated.
#
# `bun run check` runs scripts/check-i18n.ts, which flags visible text and
# user-facing attributes (placeholder, label, title, aria-label, alt) that are
# not {t('feature.key')}. Catalog parity can only audit keys that exist; this is
# what catches the string that was never made a key at all.
#
# Put a literal here ONLY when translating it would be wrong: a brand name, a
# product name, a unit symbol, an untranslated proper noun, or copy that never
# ships to a user. Everything else belongs in messages/*.toml — in EVERY locale,
# or stack.Validate fails with I18N0202.
#
# One literal per line, whitespace-collapsed, copied exactly as the checker
# prints it. `#` starts a comment. An entry nothing matches is reported as a
# note, so this file stays honest as the screens change.

# --- the scaffold's own placeholder copy ---
# +page.svelte is the page you are about to delete. When you do, delete these
# three lines too — the checker will tell you they are unused.
